    'honor.aiDown': 'Weathered the AI wave', 'honor.aiUp': 'Rode the AI wave', 'honor.tough': 'Came through the hard years',
    'honor.lic': 'Holder of {n} licenses', 'honor.kids': 'Raised {n} kids while working', 'honor.away': 'Left {home} to make a living', 'honor.plain': 'Devoted to {aJob}', 'honor.steady': 'Steady worker',
    'epi.first': 'Got placed on a team they never asked for and spent six months learning the basics.|Bought the family a small gift with the first paycheck.|The first manager was tough, but taught them how work really gets done.|The new work clothes still felt a size too big.|Half of what training covered did not survive the first week on the job.|Made a mistake on the first real assignment and replayed it the whole ride home.',
    'epi.firstSelf': 'Hands shook a little while filing the business paperwork.|Will probably never forget the first customer.|The sign went up, and the phone did not ring once that first month.',
    'epi.newJob': 'It took a while for the new coworkers to learn their name.|The old way of doing things did not work here; learned it all again.|Checked the first paystub at the new job more than once.|Kept hearing "So how did you do it at your last place?"',
    'epi.young': 'Got a first mentee and found out teaching is hard.|Was handed a big project and lost some sleep over it.|One of the people who started the same year quit. Nobody asked the real reason.|Opened a study guide on weekends, then closed it again.|A friend said "That sounds like a good job," and it felt good.|Found a spot to grab a drink with coworkers after work.|Got used to the Monday morning commute without noticing.',
    'epi.mid': 'Suddenly one of the longest-serving people at work.|Got a callback from the annual checkup for the first time.|Did not always follow what the younger staff were talking about.|More and more, got to decide how the work gets done.|Clients started asking for them by name.|More nights spent wondering "Is this it?"|The workplace changed its systems and there was a mountain to relearn.',
    'epi.late': 'Started counting the years to retirement.|A retirement-plan statement arrived in the mail.|Someone they once trained became their boss.|Started reading documents with reading glasses.|People began saying "If you have a question about this work, ask them."|Heard that someone from the same starting class had passed away.',
    'epi.senior': 'Younger coworkers keep asking about the old days.|The body complains, but it is good to have somewhere to be in the morning.|The pay is lower, but the load feels lighter.|Told a grandchild about work and got wide eyes.|Became the oldest person at work.',
    'epi.mgr': 'Talked with a team member until the last train was gone.|Caught between the bosses above and the team below, for weeks.|A team member got promoted, and it felt like their own win.|Meetings started taking more time than the actual work.|Had to give a team member hard feedback in a review.',
    'epi.irr': 'The night before a contract renewal was always restless.|Doing the same work as the full-timers, for less.|Bonus season felt a little awkward.|Someone mentioned a full-time opening once, and then never again.',
    'epi.self': 'Tax season, every year, comes with a sigh.|A big client walked away and sleep did not come easily.|New customers arrived through word of mouth.|Even on days off, work kept creeping into their head.|Setting their own prices never got easy.',
    'epi.pub': 'The annual reassignment list set the office buzzing.|After a rough day at the service desk, the walk home felt long.|Worked days on end during a disaster response.|Kept a thank-you letter from a resident in the desk drawer.',
    'epi.kids': 'Planned weeks ahead to make it to the school sports day.|Rushed through work every day to make daycare pickup.|A child asked "What do you do at work?" and the answer did not come easily.|Called in early because a child had a fever.',
    'epi.care': 'Asked the boss for time off to care for a parent.|Kept checking the phone at work in case a parent needed help.|Weekends went to driving back and forth to a parent\'s home.',
    'epi.low': 'Sunday nights started to feel heavy.|One morning, their feet would not move on the train platform.|Things they used to love stopped feeling fun.',
    'epi.skill': 'Started getting work because people asked for them by name.|Was invited to speak at an industry meetup.|Heard that the new hires were copying their way of working.',

